The vts module counts what goes through nginx -- per server, per upstream,
per cache zone, per filter -- and serves the counters as JSON, as a
Prometheus exposition or as an HTML page.  Counters live in shared memory,
so every worker contributes to the same numbers, and a control interface
resets or deletes single zones without a reload.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their VTS option is enabled.
